   "notes": "Habit four: before the meeting, run through this five-point list. First, read your titles in order: does each one state a single message? Second, scan for text-heavy slides and move the details into your notes. Third, show the deck at full screen and step back from your monitor, or ask a colleague, to check it can be read. Fourth, check that fonts, colors and title positions are consistent. Finally, practice out loud at least once with a timer. Saying it aloud shows you where slides are unclear and whether you fit your time slot. So what do the four habits add up to?"
